message.content:
This is a plastic bag with an integral extruded closure (zipper-type), made of laminate where polyethylene is 80% by weight. HTSUS 3923.21 covers sacks and bags (including cones) of polymers of ethylene. The subheading 3923.21.00 is split into 3923.21.0085 (other) and 3923.21.0095 (other, other) in the current schedule, and I recall 3923.21.0085 as "Other" and 3923.21.0095 as the older entry for other. The current structure is 3923.21.00 with statistical suffixes 3923.21.0085 ("Other") and 3923.21.0095 ("Other"), where 3923.21.0080 covers "Retail packaging" sacks/bags (hmm, 3923.21.0080 is "Sterilization pouches"?).

I believe the 3923.21 breakdown is: 3923.21.0020 (Sterilization pouches/ bags of a kind...), 3923.21.0080 (Other: Containing by weight 80% or more polyethylene?), 3923.21.0085 (Other: Other), 3923.21.0095 (Other). Given the 80% polyethylene and the "of polymers of ethylene" language, 3923.21.0085 is the usual answer in CBP rulings for such bags.

{"hts_code": "3923.21.0085", "reason": "Plastic bag with integral extruded closure for packaging, of a laminate that is 80% polyethylene by weight, is classified as a sack or bag of polymers of ethylene under heading 3923, subheading 3923.21."}
